=base:main-content.cmark

# About

tramaj is written by Lucas DiCioccio, who also writes about it, and about
the other tools it grows alongside, on his blog at
[dicioccio.fr](https://dicioccio.fr/). The source is on
[GitHub](https://github.com/lucasdicioccio/tramaj).

## Related sites

- [Kitchen Sink](https://kitchensink-tech.github.io/) — the static-site
  generator this site is made with. Its templating sections are evaluated
  by `tramaj-hs`, the Haskell implementation of tramaj.
- [salmon](https://lucasdicioccio.github.io/salmon/) — a Haskell toolkit
  for describing infrastructure as a graph of idempotent operations. Its
  site is built with Kitchen Sink too.
- [agents-exe](https://lucasdicioccio.github.io/agents-exe/) — a runner
  for LLM agents, with a Kitchen Sink site as well.
- [dicioccio.fr](https://dicioccio.fr/) — the author's blog, also built
  with Kitchen Sink.

